  "meaning": "Native summaries of the lithium silo clock family (lithium-silo-clock-fixtures.ts) in Factorio 2.1.21: the lithium plate build with a rocket silo as a chest, on its selected clock (3 output swings) in two build orders, on 1 output swing and on 7, each with the clock lithium-silo-clock.generation.test.ts pins. The standard protocol: the holmium plates cut for 2 periods, the output blocked for 4, the holmium plates cut again; the silo, which holds at most 250 lithium, is empty in each cut. The harness warms the build up for 3600 ticks without a clock, so the silo is full when the clock starts. The clock with 7 output swings does not hold in the game: two output inserters drop onto belts that side-load onto the shared output belt, which the config describes as one belt.",
